# Scout Agent System — Background Reasoning Watchers

## Context

NUDIMMUD has a rich hook lifecycle (SessionStart → PreToolUse → PostToolUse → Stop) but no background reasoning layer. When Claude takes an action, nothing is double-checking it in parallel. This plan builds **three scout agents** (ARGUS, CASSANDRA, HERMES) + one instant heuristic checker (CASSANDRA-LITE) that auto-join every session, reason over tool calls, and inject findings into the next turn via the existing `emitContext` / `hookSpecificOutput` mechanism already used by `pre-tool-use.js`.

---

## Architecture

```
PostToolUse (async)
  └─ scout-spawn.js (async: true)
       ├─ cassandra-lite.js (sync, instant regex/heuristics) → emitContext immediately if risk found
       ├─ spawn ARGUS background (claude haiku) → scout-bus.json
       └─ spawn CASSANDRA background (claude haiku) → scout-bus.json
       [HERMES spawns only on Write/Edit tool calls — context drift]

PreToolUse (sync) — runs BEFORE existing pre-tool-use.js
  └─ scout-inject.js
       └─ reads scout-bus.json → unconsumed entries → emitContext → marks consumed
```

**Injection vector:** `process.stderr.write(JSON.stringify({ hookSpecificOutput: { hookEventName: 'PreToolUse', additionalContext: msg } }))` — exact pattern from `pre-tool-use.js:33-36`.

**Peer communication:** Each scout receives the last 5 unconsumed bus entries as context before reasoning, so they build on each other's findings.

---

## Scout Definitions

| Scout | Trigger | Model | Purpose |
|-------|---------|-------|---------|
| **ARGUS** | Write, Edit, Agent, Bash | haiku | Logic consistency — contradictions, off-task drift, wrong assumptions |
| **CASSANDRA** | Write, Edit, Bash | haiku | Risk prediction — destructive ops, irreversible actions, T7 violations |
| **CASSANDRA-LITE** | All tools | pure JS | Instant regex — `rm -rf`, `--force`, `T7`, `DROP TABLE`, `chmod 777` |
| **HERMES** | Write, Edit only | haiku | Context drift — flags when Claude is drifting from original task scope |

**THEMIS** (quality scout) deferred to v2 — overlaps with OBLITERATUS-QA which already exists.

